From: Florian Maurer <maurer@fh-aachen.de>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 07:01:29 +0000
Subject: Revert "kernel: modules: load e1000e driver during pre-init stage"

This reverts commit f22f533ebcbc0f7123481a01abd3a547f0232260.

Loading e1000e in the pre-init stage moves it in front of r8169, e1000,
8139cp, e100 and other Ethernet drivers in the module load order, so on
x86 devices combining an e1000e NIC with one of those, eth0 and eth1 are
switched compared to OpenWrt 24.10 and Gluon assigns the interface roles
to the wrong ports after an upgrade from v2025.1.x.

Gluon does not need the early load: the pre-init renaming by device path
from board.json only applies to a handful of x86 boards, which behaved
the same way on 24.10. Keep the 24.10 load order until the interface
roles follow the device paths on all devices (see 020-interfaces), after
which this revert can be dropped.

Assisted-by: claude:opus-5

diff --git a/package/kernel/linux/modules/netdevices.mk b/package/kernel/linux/modules/netdevices.mk
index 42fc497e8d24dbb7aad42e902bcd72b93b744fe4..0396520f7aebb10f2fb84813fb4cd815350cbc1c 100644
--- a/package/kernel/linux/modules/netdevices.mk
+++ b/package/kernel/linux/modules/netdevices.mk
@@ -1292,7 +1292,7 @@ define KernelPackage/e1000e
   DEPENDS:=@PCIE_SUPPORT +kmod-ptp
   KCONFIG:=CONFIG_E1000E
   FILES:=$(LINUX_DIR)/drivers/net/ethernet/intel/e1000e/e1000e.ko
-  AUTOLOAD:=$(call AutoProbe,e1000e,1)
+  AUTOLOAD:=$(call AutoProbe,e1000e)
   MODPARAMS.e1000e:= \
     IntMode=1 \
     InterruptThrottleRate=4,4,4,4,4,4,4,4
